1
00:04:08,181 --> 00:04:14,181
Avalon High is a fantasy, family, drama film directed by Stuart Gillard.

2
00:08:16,363 --> 00:08:22,363
Elaine "Ellie" Harrison has just moved from Minnesota to Annapolis, Maryland while her parents take
a year-long sabbatical to continue their medieval studies in nearby Washington D.C.

3
00:12:24,545 --> 00:12:30,545
Her new high school, Avalon High, seems like a typical high school with the stereotypical students: Lance the jock, Jennifer the
cheerleader, Marco, the bad boy/desperado, and Will, the senior class president, quarterback, and all around good guy.

4
00:16:32,727 --> 00:16:38,727
But not everyone at Avalon High is who they
appear to be, not even Ellie herself.

5
00:20:40,909 --> 00:20:46,909
Eventually, it becomes apparent that Avalon High is a situation
where the ancient Arthurian legend is repeating itself.

6
00:24:49,090 --> 00:24:55,090
Allie Pennington, played by Britt Robertson.

7
00:28:57,272 --> 00:29:03,272
Will Wagner, played by Gregg Sulkin.

8
00:33:05,454 --> 00:33:11,454
Miles, played by Joey Pollari.

9
00:37:13,636 --> 00:37:19,636
Marco, played by Devon Graye.

10
00:41:21,818 --> 00:41:27,818
Jen, played by Molly C. Quinn.

11
00:45:30,000 --> 00:45:36,000
Mr. Moore, played by Steve Valentine.

12
00:49:38,181 --> 00:49:44,181
Avalon High is a 2010 American fantasy television film, a Disney Channel Original
Movie, and a loose adaptation of Meg Cabot’s 2005 novel of the same name.

13
00:53:46,363 --> 00:53:52,363
Directed by Stuart Gillard, the film stars Britt Robertson as Allie Pennington, a high school student
who discovers she may be the reincarnation of a legendary figure from Arthurian myth.

14
00:57:54,545 --> 00:58:00,545
The cast also includes Gregg Sulkin, Joey Pollari, Devon Graye, and Molly C.

15
01:02:02,727 --> 01:02:08,727
The second Disney Channel Original Movie directed by Gillard after Twitches Too
(2007), its teleplay was written by Gillian Horvath and Lee Goldberg.

16
01:06:10,909 --> 01:06:16,909
Set in a modern-day high school, the story reimagines key characters from
Arthurian legend as contemporary teenagers caught in a prophecy.

17
01:10:19,090 --> 01:10:25,090
Filming took place in New Zealand in mid-2010, with the production
emphasizing themes of destiny, identity, and mythological legacy.

18
01:14:27,272 --> 01:14:33,272
Avalon High premiered on Disney Channel in the United States on November 12, 2010, and was later released
in Australia and New Zealand on January 22, 2011, and in the United Kingdom on January 28.

19
01:18:35,454 --> 01:18:41,454
The film received mixed critical reception, with reviewers noting its accessible premise for
younger audiences but critiquing its departure from the book's original narrative.

20
01:22:43,636 --> 01:22:49,636
The film explores themes of high school, based on novel or
book, prophecy, camelot, reincarnation.

21
01:26:51,818 --> 01:26:57,818
The tone is emotional.
